  "code": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n\n    alpha = float(extra.get('alpha', extra.get('hyperparams', {}).get('alpha', 1.0)))\n    hp = extra.get('hyperparams', {})\n    scale = float(hp.get('scale', 1.5057527233517845))\n    beta = float(hp.get('beta', 0.1))\n    tau = float(hp.get('tau', 2.0))\n\n    cost_a = batch['cost_a']\n    cost_b = batch['cost_b']\n    gap = (cost_b - cost_a).detach()\n\n    # Smooth, bounded margin from cost gap to avoid overly shifting the logit.\n    margin = beta * ops.tanh(gap / tau)\n\n    x = alpha * scale * (lpw - lpl) - margin\n    x = ops.clamp(x, -20.0, 20.0)\n    loss = -ops.logsigmoid(x)\n    if weight is not None:\n        loss = loss * weight\n    return loss.mean()",
  "theoretical_basis": "Pairwise logistic (Bradley-Terry style) objective with an additive, bounded margin that depends on auxiliary preference strength (cost gap). Using a detached, squashed margin keeps gradients focused on log-prob differences while encoding that larger cost gaps should correspond to larger separation.",
