  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_000_cost_tuned_scale_061",
  "intuition": "Tune only the `scale` applied to the log-probability margin (lpw - lpl). In this loss, x = alpha*scale*(lpw-lpl) - 0.1*gap and then is clamped before logsigmoid. If `scale` is too low, the preference signal is weak relative to the fixed cost term and gradients become small; if too high, x hits the clamp more often and saturates logsigmoid, also reducing useful gradient. A moderate increase from ~0.54 to ~0.61 strengthens the ranking signal while staying less likely to saturate given the [-20, 20] clamp.",
